00:12:42.540 --> 00:12:44.060
It would be completely empty.

00:12:44.060 --> 00:12:45.600
Like wiping a hard drive.

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:50.220
Destroy the brain, and Wade Wilson as we know him ceases to be.

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:51.320
Kind of like a zombie.

00:12:51.320 --> 00:12:53.260
I think Deadpool would appreciate that sort of reference.

00:12:53.260 --> 00:12:54.260
In the end, I guess it just

00:12:54.260 --> 00:12:55.310
goes to show

00:12:55.310 --> 00:12:59.610
often times good science doesn't result in good movies.

00:12:59.610 --> 00:13:02.760
But, hey! That's just a theory!

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:04.680
A film theory!

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:06.300
Aaand cut!

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:09.959
And before you go, a huge thank
you once again to Bill and Melinda Gates

00:13:09.959 --> 00:13:13.050
for reaching out to me to pontificate a bit about superheroes.

00:13:13.050 --> 00:13:15.750
Now that I'm wrapping up this video, I
recommend taking the next five minutes

00:13:15.750 --> 00:13:18.790
to read their annual letter by clicking
the link in the description.

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:21.210
If we're talking about real life superheroes,

00:13:21.210 --> 00:13:25.080
then the Gateses are two people who definitely fall in that category.

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:28.500
Using their global influence to inspire
others to make a positive difference in

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:29.560
the world around them.

00:13:29.560 --> 00:13:32.640
So read the letter and get inspired to make your mark on the world.

00:13:32.640 --> 00:13:36.800
Though you may not be the person who cures cancer or brings electricity to Central Africa.

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:39.720
Oddly specific reference I know
but it's in the letter.

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:43.079
Remember that being a hero doesn't require something big.

00:13:43.079 --> 00:13:46.099
You can be someone else's hero by just saying or

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:48.360
doing something small for someone else.

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:51.000
So go ahead today tell your parents that you love them.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:52.960
Tell a co-worker you appreciate them.

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:56.120
Take some time to get to know the quiet kid who sits alone at lunch.

00:13:56.130 --> 00:13:59.850
The world will be a better place for it
one person at a time. And finally, enough

00:13:59.850 --> 00:14:02.040
sappiness, but let me know in the
comments if you could have one

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:03.930
superpower what would you want?

00:14:03.930 --> 00:14:05.830
If you say flying, I don't blame you.

00:14:05.830 --> 00:14:08.180
It's in my top three, along with healing factor,

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:12.100
and, I don't know, uh... the power of musical theater!

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:13.780
They shall call me...

00:14:13.780 --> 00:14:15.680
Show Tunes Lad!

00:14:15.820 --> 00:14:16.620
Or something.

00:14:16.709 --> 00:14:18.289
Now if you'll excuse me, I gotta go.

00:14:18.289 --> 00:14:19.340
Crisp high five?

00:14:19.349 --> 00:14:21.349
Crisp high five!

